+# Feature Specification: Validate task input
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-11 | **Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Reject invalid titles, priorities and tags when a task is added, renamed or tagged.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Bad input is refused with a clear error (Priority: P1)
+Screens pass raw user input to the list. The list refuses invalid input with an error saying what is wrong, and the list stays unchanged.
+
+**Independent Test**: call add/rename/tag with each invalid input; check the error and that the list is identical afterwards.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** any list, **When** a task is added or renamed with an empty or spaces-only title, **Then** it is refused.
+2. **When** the title (trimmed) is over 120 characters, **Then** it is refused; exactly 120 is accepted.
+3. **When** a task is added with a priority other than low, normal, high, **Then** it is refused.
+4. **When** a task is added with, or tagged with, a tag that is empty or contains a space, **Then** it is refused.
+5. **When** any of the above is refused, **Then** no task, tag, title or timestamp changes and no id is consumed.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: Titles are checked after trimming: non-empty, at most 120 characters.
+- **FR-002**: Priority, when given, must be one of low, normal, high.
+- **FR-003**: Tags must be non-empty and contain no whitespace.
+- **FR-004**: Checks apply to add (title, priority, every tag), rename (new title) and tag (tag).
+- **FR-005**: Refusals use a new error code `invalid-input` with a message naming the problem.
+- **FR-006**: A refused operation leaves the list unchanged.
+
+## Assumptions
+- "Space" means any whitespace character. Tags are not trimmed. Untag/find are not validated.
